<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<definitions xmlns="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL" xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI" xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC" xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" id="defs_P_8_9" targetNamespace="http://tim-method.example/utility-wam/1.0" exporter="Utility WAM Industry Process Reference" exporterVersion="2026-08-28">
  <process id="P_8_9" name="8.9 Conduct pipeline public awareness" isExecutable="false">
    <documentation>Three of the four processes are drawn. 8.9.1 the written programme is SPEC and is what this cycle runs against.

THE AUDIENCE IS A SPATIAL QUESTION BEFORE IT IS A COMMUNICATIONS ONE. The affected public is defined by proximity to the system, so the list is built from the network footprint and NOT from the customer list. A resident who is not a customer is still affected public, and building the audience from billing data quietly drops exactly the people the rule is about.

49 CFR 192.616 requires a written continuing public education programme following the guidance in API RP 1162, and names four audiences: the affected public, emergency officials, local public officials and excavators. The section sets no interval figure of its own - the delivery frequencies come from the RP, which is recommended practice from a member-gated body and not law in itself. Where the programme departs from it, the departure and its rationale are recorded.

REACH IS NOT EFFECTIVENESS. 192.616 requires the effectiveness of the programme to be evaluated, and reach can be read off the delivery record while comprehension cannot - it requires asking the audience. A programme that reports only what it sent has not evaluated anything, and the flow draws the two as separate tasks for that reason.

Gas only. No electric distribution public awareness obligation of this kind exists.</documentation>
    <laneSet id="P_8_9_lanes">
      <lane id="l_89_prog" name="Public awareness programme">
        <flowNodeRef>n_89_start</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_89_prog</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_89_foot</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_89_aud</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_89_reach</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_89_un</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_89_rch</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_89_comp</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_89_ev</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_89_ret</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_89_end</flowNodeRef>
      </lane>
      <lane id="l_89_del" name="Delivery">
        <flowNodeRef>n_89_del</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_89_sup</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_89_sup2</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_89_cap</flowNodeRef>
      </lane>
    </laneSet>
    <startEvent id="n_89_start" name="The programme cycle opens"><timerEventDefinition id="n_89_start_td"/></startEvent>
    <receiveTask id="n_89_prog" name="Take the written programme and its message set"><documentation>8.9.1, SPEC. 192.616, following API RP 1162.</documentation></receiveTask>
    <serviceTask id="n_89_foot" name="Take the network footprint and the areas it passes"><documentation>8.9.2. Spatial. NOT the customer list.</documentation></serviceTask>
    <userTask id="n_89_aud" name="Identify the four audiences and size each"><documentation>8.9.2. Affected public, emergency officials, local public officials, excavators - named by the section, not chosen by the operator.</documentation></userTask>
    <exclusiveGateway id="n_89_reach" name="A working reach method exists"/>
    <serviceTask id="n_89_un" name="Record the audience as unreachable"><documentation>8.9.2. An effectiveness finding for 8.9.4, not a quiet exclusion from the population.</documentation></serviceTask>
    <userTask id="n_89_del" name="Deliver the baseline messages at the stated frequency"><documentation>8.9.3. The frequencies are the RP's; 192.616 sets none.</documentation></userTask>
    <exclusiveGateway id="n_89_sup" name="A supplemental trigger has arisen"/>
    <userTask id="n_89_sup2" name="Deliver the supplemental messages"><documentation>8.9.3. A different obligation. Delivering more baseline does not discharge it.</documentation></userTask>
    <serviceTask id="n_89_cap" name="Capture what was sent, to whom, how and when"><documentation>8.9.3. Undeliverable contacts are a finding, carried forward to the next audience identification.</documentation></serviceTask>
    <businessRuleTask id="n_89_rch" name="Measure reach from the delivery record"><documentation>8.9.4. What was sent and received.</documentation></businessRuleTask>
    <userTask id="n_89_comp" name="Measure comprehension by asking the audience"><documentation>8.9.4. Cannot be read off the delivery record. A programme reporting only reach has not evaluated effectiveness.</documentation></userTask>
    <serviceTask id="n_89_ev" name="Evaluate against the programme objectives"><documentation>8.9.4. 192.616 requires the effectiveness to be evaluated.</documentation></serviceTask>
    <sendTask id="n_89_ret" name="Retain the evidence and return the findings"><documentation>8.9.4. Message content, audience list, delivery record and evaluation - what a regulator inspects, not the evaluation alone.</documentation></sendTask>
    <endEvent id="n_89_end" name="Cycle evaluated and evidenced"/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_89_start_n_89_prog" sourceRef="n_89_start" targetRef="n_89_prog" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_89_prog_n_89_foot" sourceRef="n_89_prog" targetRef="n_89_foot" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_89_foot_n_89_aud" sourceRef="n_89_foot" targetRef="n_89_aud" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_89_aud_n_89_reach" sourceRef="n_89_aud" targetRef="n_89_reach" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_89_reach_n_89_un" sourceRef="n_89_reach" targetRef="n_89_un" name="no reliable method"><conditionExpression xsi:type="tFormalExpression"><![CDATA[reachable = false]]></conditionExpression></sequenceFlow>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_89_un_n_89_rch" sourceRef="n_89_un" targetRef="n_89_rch" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_89_reach_n_89_del" sourceRef="n_89_reach" targetRef="n_89_del" name="reachable"/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_89_del_n_89_sup" sourceRef="n_89_del" targetRef="n_89_sup" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_89_sup_n_89_sup2" sourceRef="n_89_sup" targetRef="n_89_sup2" name="trigger arisen"><conditionExpression xsi:type="tFormalExpression"><![CDATA[supplemental = true]]></conditionExpression></sequenceFlow>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_89_sup2_n_89_cap" sourceRef="n_89_sup2" targetRef="n_89_cap" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_89_sup_n_89_cap" sourceRef="n_89_sup" targetRef="n_89_cap" name="baseline only"/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_89_cap_n_89_rch" sourceRef="n_89_cap" targetRef="n_89_rch" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_89_rch_n_89_comp" sourceRef="n_89_rch" targetRef="n_89_comp" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_89_comp_n_89_ev" sourceRef="n_89_comp" targetRef="n_89_ev" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_89_ev_n_89_ret" sourceRef="n_89_ev" targetRef="n_89_ret" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_89_ret_n_89_end" sourceRef="n_89_ret" targetRef="n_89_end" name=""/>
  </process>
